\alias{LearnerCptXGBoostAFT}
\title{Extreme Gradient Boosting AFT Changepoint Learner}
\description{
Learns a penalty function for changepoint detection from weak labels via
gradient boosted trees with the accelerated failure time objective
(\code{objective = "survival:aft"}) of \code{\link[xgboost:xgb.train]{xgboost::xgb.train()}}.

At train time, each sequence is summarized into a numeric feature vector and
the labels are converted into an interval of admissible \code{log(lambda)}
penalties (the segment path is fitted per sequence, scored against the label
regions, and the error curve inverted). The AFT loss fits these
interval-censored targets directly, so unlike
\link{mlr_learners_changepoint.intregrcv} it also trains when no label gives a
finite lower (or upper) penalty limit.

At predict time, the learner returns \code{response}, the predicted \code{log(lambda)}
per sequence.

The label solvers are chosen by the task's \code{label_type}:
\code{"changepoint"} uses \code{\link[changepoint:cpt.mean]{changepoint::cpt.mean()}}, \code{"peak"} uses
\code{\link[PeakSegOptimal:PeakSegPDPAchrom]{PeakSegOptimal::PeakSegPDPAchrom()}}.
}
